            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 2,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 2s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Arabic for a pump, then the Arabic for to tow."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: رخصة",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "رخصة — rukhṣa — \"a licence; a permit\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "عند أختي رخصة (rukhṣa) قيادة جديدة. ʿinda ukhtī rukhṣat qiyāda jadīda. My sister has a new driving licence."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "رخصة (rukhṣa) is built on the native Arabic root r-kh-ṣ, \"to be soft, easy, cheap\" (Lane). A rukhṣa is an easing: a permission. It shares its root with rakhīṣ, \"cheap\"."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for getting around."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 4,
          "type": "guided-production",
          "title": "Guided Practice",
          "segments": [
            {
